        object TASMemo1: TTASMemo
          Left = 2
          Top = 2
          Width = 611
          Height = 325
          TabStop = False
          Font.Charset = DEFAULT_CHARSET
          Font.Color = clWindowText
          Font.Height = -15
          Font.Name = 'Arial'
          Font.Style = []
          Lines.Strings = (
            ''
            'Please Read Before Proceeding'
            '-------------------------------------------'
            ''
            'What SM-J-C does'
            '-------------------------------'
            ''
            
              'SM-J-C enables you to reconcile your inventory data files.  Ther' +
              'e are 2 levels of '
            'reconciliation that can be performed:'
            ''
            
              'If you have never run UT-K-I, Fix Binary Zeroes, before. You sho' +
              'uld do so for the Following '
            
              'files: BKICMSTR, MTICMSTR, BKICLOC, INVTXN, and CLASS process en' +
              'sure that there '
            'are no binary zeroes in your data.'
            ''
            'MASTER LEVEL'
            
              '     Synchronizes the Inventory Master (BKICMSTR, MTICMSTR), Loc' +
              'ation'
            
              '     Master (BKICLOCM), Location Detail (BKICLOC), Class/Locatio' +
              'n (CLASS),'
            
              '     Class Master (CLASMSTR), and LIFO/FIFO Buckets (DBAFIFO) fi' +
              'les to'
            '     and between each other.'
            ''
            'TRANSACTION LEVEL'
            
              '     Reconciles the Inventory Master (BKICMSTR) and Location Det' +
              'ail'
            
              '     (BKICLOC) files to the Inventory Transactions (INVTXN) file' +
              '.'
            
              '     You will be able to choose whether you want to force the Tr' +
              'ansactions'
            
              '     to equal the Master file data, or vice-versa.  These are th' +
              'e same'
            
              '     transactions used in the IN-E (Print Inventory Transactions' +
              ') report.'
            ''
            'If you run a Transaction Level, run a Master Level as well'
            
              '----------------------------------------------------------------' +
              '-------------'
            
              'It is highly recommended, if you wish to perform a Transaction L' +
              'evel reconciliation, that '
            
              'you also perform a Master Level reconciliation at the same time.' +
              '  This is because the '
            
              'accuracy of the Transaction Level reconciliation is highly depen' +
              'dent on the accuracy of '
            'the Master Level files.'
            ''
            'The Reconciliation Report'
            '----------------------------------'
            
              'Both reconciliation Levels will generate a report detailing any ' +
              'changes that may have been '
            
              'made (you will be able to choose whether to print or display the' +
              ' report after the '
            
              'reconciliation process is complete).  The far left column will d' +
              'isplay an "*" for items that '
            
              'SM-J-C was unable to resolve or that need more attention on your' +
              ' part.  This column will '
            
              'also display a "$"  sign for items that affect inventory value i' +
              'n the General Ledger.'
            ''
            
              'You can also choose to run the reconciliation in '#39'report-only'#39' m' +
              'ode. '
            ''
            
              'In this case, no changes will be made to your data.  Only a repo' +
              'rt detailing anticipated '
            
              'changes will be generated, so that you may preview what will be ' +
              'done without actually '
            'changing anything.'
            
              'Please bear in mind, however, that when you subsequently run the' +
              ' recon-ciliation '#8216'for '
            
              'real'#39', the actual changes made may not exactly match the initial' +
              ' report.  This is because '
            
              'changes made later in the process are dependent upon changes mad' +
              'e earlier in the '
            
              'process.  Thus problems fixed in early steps may mean that chang' +
              'es the report has '
            
              'indicated are needed in later steps are no longer necessary.  Al' +
              'so, some of the anticipated '
            
              'adjustments may look strange because they are using nubmers that' +
              ' have not yet really '
            'been fixed in the earlier steps.'
            ''
            
              'Another factor contributing to differences between anticipated a' +
              'nd actual changes could '
            
              'be the actions of other users posting inventory transactions bet' +
              'ween the time you ran the '
            
              'report and the time you actually made the reconciliation changes' +
              '.'
            ''
            'Suggested Strategy'
            '--------------------------'
            
              ' If you wish to back up your data before running SM-J-C  (never ' +
              'a bad idea), the following '
            
              'files may get changed by SM-J-C: BKICMSTR, MTICMSTR, BKICLOC, BK' +
              'ICLOCM, '
            'CLASMSTR, CLASS, DBAFIFO, and INVTXN. '
            
              'This is an extensive process and can take some time to run, depe' +
              'nding on how much '
            
              'data needs to be analyzed.  In addition it is interactive, so yo' +
              'u may be prompted for '
            
              'information during the run if SM-J-C encounters a situation that' +
              ' it cannot resolve by itself.  '
            
              'Such cases will be indicated on the "report-only" report as SM-J' +
              '-C will prompt you".'
            
              ' If you choose NOT to run in report-only mode (so that data will' +
              ' get changed), SM-J-C will '
            
              'not run if any other users are currently working in this company' +
              '.  This is done to ensure '
            
              'that SM-J-C does not encounter an inventory transaction that has' +
              ' not yet completely '
            
              'posted to all files, thus resulting in SM-J-C making an unwarran' +
              'ted adjustment.  If you run '
            
              'SM-J-C in report-only mode (where no data will get changed), you' +
              ' can do so while other '
            
              'users are working with this company.  However, the report may st' +
              'ill indicate unnecessary '
            
              'adjustments if incomplete transactions are encountered.  In this' +
              ' case you should ensure '
            
              'that other users will be doing tasks that do not affect inventor' +
              'y files.'#39
            ''
            'A suggested strategy for using SM-J-C might be as follows:'
            ''
            '1. MASTER LEVEL, REPORT-ONLY'
            
              '      Run a Master Level reconciliation, in report-only mode.  T' +
              'his will give you a feel for the '
            
              'extent of necessary changes and you can decide whether or not to' +
              ' proceed with them.'
            ''
            '2. ACTUAL MASTER LEVEL RECONCILIATION'
            ' '
            
              '      After reviewing the report, go ahead and run the Master Le' +
              'vel reconciliation '#39'for real'#39'.  '
            'You'#39'll get a second report indicating the actual changes made.'
            ' '
            '3. TRANSACTION LEVEL, REPORT-ONLY'
            ' '
            
              '      If you wish to run a Transaction reconciliation, go ahead ' +
              'and run it in report-only mode '
            'if you would like to preview the changes.'
            ''
            '4. ACTUAL TRANSACTION LEVEL RECONCILIATION'
            
              '     After reviewing the report, go ahead and start the '#39'for-rea' +
              'l'#39' Transaction Level '
            
              'reconciliation.   If other users are on the system, and may have' +
              ' affected inventory files '
            
              'between the time you ran the Master Level reconciliation and now' +
              ', you probably should '
            
              'choose to run the Master Level reconciliation again at the same ' +
              'time you choose which '
            
              'Transaction Level method (A or B) to use.  The Master Level reco' +
              'nciliation will get run first '
            
              '(should not take as long as the first time), followed immediatel' +
              'y by the Transaction '
            
              'reconciliation.  It is possible to run both the Master and Trans' +
              'action Levels in report-only '
            
              'mode at the same time.  However, the Transaction report will be ' +
              'more meaningful if you '
            
              'have first run the Master Level reconciliation '#39'for real'#39'.  You ' +
              'can also run Master and '
            
              'Transaction '#39'for real'#39' at the same time.  The Master gets run fi' +
              'rst so that the Transaction '
            'Level will be based on accurate data.'
            ' '
            'What does the Master Level reconciliation do?'
            ' -------------------------------------------------------------'
            ' '
            
              'NOTE: The information in this section is provided for technical ' +
              'reference only. You do not  '
            
              'need to know it to effectively use SM-J-C and can skip this sect' +
              'ion if desired. '
            ' '
            
              '*  Deletes any blank records in the BKICMSTR, MTICMSTR, BKICLOC,' +
              ' CLASMSTR, '
            'CLASS, INVTXN, and DBAFIFO files.'
            ' '
            
              '*  Checks BKICLOCM (Location Master file).  If it has no records' +
              ', adds one for the default '
            
              '(Inventory Defaults) location.  If there are records, but none f' +
              'or the default (Inventory '
            
              'Defaults) location, adds one for that location.  Deletes any dup' +
              'licate BKICLOCM records.'
            ''
            
              '*  Checks CLASMSTR (Class Master file).  If it has no records, c' +
              'reates one for Class '
            '"DFLT".  Deletes any duplicate CLASMSTR records.'
            ''
            
              '*  Deletes any duplicate records found in CLASS (Class/Location ' +
              'file). Any Classes in '
            
              'CLASS that do not exist in CLASMSTR are added to CLASMSTR. Any L' +
              'ocations in '
            
              'CLASS that do not exist in BKICLOCM are changed to the default L' +
              'ocation.'
            ''
            
              '*  Deletes any "stranded"  BKICLOC records (records without a co' +
              'rresponding '
            'BKICMSTR record for that Part.) '
            ''
            
              '*  Resets the Active Status to "R" (recovered) for any missing M' +
              'TICMSTR records.'
            ''
            
              ' The following are done for every Part within the range specifie' +
              'd by user: '
            ' '
            
              '*  Checks important BKICMSTR (Inventory Master file) fields.  If' +
              ' Type is not valid '
            
              '(NRMFABLTKO), checks if Type in the MTICMSTR file (Auxiliary Inv' +
              'entory Master) for this '
            
              'part is valid.  If so, changes Type in BKICMSTR to that value.  ' +
              'If not, sets BKICMSTR Type '
            
              'to '#39'R'#39'.  If the Stock U/M in BKICMSTR is blank, sets that to be ' +
              'the same as MTICMSTR '
            
              'Selling U/M (if that is also blank, then sets Stock U/M to '#39'EA'#39')' +
              '. '
            ''
            
              '*  If the BKICMSTR Class is not valid (not found in CLASMSTR fil' +
              'e), tries to use the '
            
              'MTICMSTR Class.  If that is also not valid, creates a new record' +
              ' in CLASMSTR for the '
            
              'BKICMSTR Class.  If the BKICMSTR Class is blank, sets BKICMSTR C' +
              'lass to be the first '
            
              'Class found in CLASMSTR instead of creating a blank CLASMSTR rec' +
              'ord.'
            ''
            
              '*  If the MTICMSTR record for a given Item No. is missing, creat' +
              'es it. Uses Class, Type, '
            
              'Description, from BKICMSTR.  Sets Purchase U/M and Selling U/M t' +
              'o be same as '
            
              'BKICMSTR Stock U/M.  Sets Active Flag to Y, Purchase Conversion ' +
              'to 1.00.  Sets the '
            'MRP Flag and the Expedite/Delay Buffers to the MD-I defaults.'
            ' '
            
              '*  If Class, Type, or Desc in MTICMSTR are not the same as in BK' +
              'ICMSTR, changes '
            
              'them in MTICMSTR.  If the MTICMSTR Purchase Conversion Factor is' +
              ' zero, sets it 1.00.  '
            
              'If the MTICMSTR Purchase U/M or Selling U/M are blamk, makes the' +
              'm the same as '
            
              'Stock U/M from BKICMSTR.  If the MRP Flag in MTICMSTR is blank, ' +
              'sets it to the MD-I '
            'default setting.'
            ' '
            
              '*  Deletes any duplicate BKICMSTR and MTICMSTR records the Part ' +
              'may have. '
            ''
            
              '*  Checks Location records (BKICLOC) for the Part.  If the Part ' +
              'does not have any '
            
              'BKICLOC records, creates one using the Inventory Defaults defaul' +
              't location code. '
            ' '
            
              '*  Makes sure that there is a matching BKICLOCM record for each ' +
              'BKICLOC location for '
            
              'that Part.  If not, Merges the IBKICLOCM record into the defualt' +
              ' location.'
            ' '
            '*  Merges any duplicate BKICLOC records.'
            ' '
            
              '*  If the Part is Type N ,K, L, T, B, or O and Units on Hand (UO' +
              'H), Total Value (TOTVL), or '
            
              'Average Cost (AVGC) in BKICMSTR are not zero, resets these numbe' +
              'rs to zero.  Then, if '
            
              'any of the BKICLOC records for the Part have a non-zero UOH, res' +
              'ets UOH for that '
            'location to zero. '
            ''
            
              '*  Rebuilds unit counts (except UOH) for each location (BKICLOC ' +
              'record) for Part from '
            
              'open orders within the system:  Units on SO and Backorder from o' +
              'pen SO'#39's, units on PO '
            
              'and in QC from open PO'#39's, and units on WO, in WIP, and Allocated' +
              ', from open Work '
            
              'Orders.  Then, checks to be sure the BKICMSTR and MTICMSTR total' +
              's for each of these '
            
              'unit counts equals the sum of the BKICLOC unit counts for all lo' +
              'cations for the Part. If not, '
            
              'the BKICMSTR/MTICMSTR totals are changed.  Finally, Units Availa' +
              'ble (AVAIL) in '
            
              'MTICMSTR is recalculated from the unit totals (the exception rep' +
              'ort will NOT print a line if '
            'this last calculation results in a change).'
            ' '
            ''
            ''
            '  What does the Method A Transaction Level reconciliation do?'
            
              '  --------------------------------------------------------------' +
              '--------------------'
            ''
            
              '  Use Method A to make the INVTXN (IN-E) transactions match the ' +
              'master inventory files.'
            ''
            'These are the steps performed by Method A:'
            ''
            
              '*  Deletes any INVTXN records whose transaction type is not ASPJ' +
              'WIQTGR. Also deletes '
            
              'any INVTXN records where a corresponding record for the part doe' +
              's not exist in '
            'BKICMSTR. '
            ''
            '*  For Type RFAM parts:'
            ''
            
              '1. If there are no INVTXN records at all for the part, creates o' +
              'ne for each location '
            '(BKICLOC record) where UOH for the part is not zero. '
            ''
            
              '2. Adds up the INVTXN records to get a UOH total by location for' +
              ' part. '
            ''
            
              '3. If any of the location totals are non-zero, but there is no m' +
              'atching BKICLOC record for '
            
              'that location, it creates an offsetting INVTXN record for that l' +
              'ocation.'
            ''
            
              '4. If UOH total for location according to INVTXN does not match ' +
              'UOH of the BKICLOC '
            'record, creates an adjusting INVTXN entry.  '
            '        '
            
              '5. If there are no INVTXN records for one of the BKICLOC locatio' +
              'ns, creates a new '
            'INVTXN record.'
            '   '
            '  What does the Method B Transaction Level reconciliation do?'
            
              '  --------------------------------------------------------------' +
              '-------------------'
            '   '
            
              'Use Method B to make the master inventory files match the INVTXN' +
              ' (IN-E) transactions.  '
            ''
            'These are the steps performed by Method B:                '
            ''
            
              '*  Deletes any INVTXN records whose transaction type is not ASPJ' +
              'WIQT.     '
            ''
            
              '*  If a part has transactions but no BKICMSTR record, lets user ' +
              'choose to create the '
            'BKICMSTR record (on-the-fly, via IN-B), or delete the trxns.'
            ''
            
              '*  Changes the BKICLOC UOH total for each location to match the ' +
              'trxns UOH total for '
            'every location. Creates the BKICLOC records if needed.      '
            ''
            '*  Changes UOH in BKICMSTR to match changes made to BKICLOC.'
            ''
            
              '*  Makes a second pass to zero out UOH (in BKICMSTR and all BKIC' +
              'LOC locations) for '
            'parts that do not have any transactions.')
          ParentFont = False
          ReadOnly = True
          ScrollBars = ssVertical
          TabOrder = 1
          DispPrgLoc = -1
